values ('e9f0a1b2-3c4d-4e99-8f89-9a0b1c2d3e09', 'u-s-history-i-to-1877', 'U.S. History I (to 1877)', 'This foundational undergraduate History course surveys North American and U.S. history from Indigenous worlds and European colonization through the Civil War and Reconstruction. The curriculum provides deep coverage of Indigenous sovereignty, Atlantic worlds, slavery and race, political economy, gender and reform, settler colonialism, emancipation, Reconstruction, and primary-source research.');

